1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,074
Teacher midterm practice, question 2.

2
00:00:03,694 --> 00:00:06,754
In Figure X, what are the Miller indices of plane B?

3
00:00:08,454 --> 00:00:11,563
Plane B is vertical, so it runs parallel to z and

4
00:00:11,563 --> 00:00:14,731
never meets it: that intercept is infinity.

5
00:00:14,731 --> 00:00:19,072
The marking key measures the plane from the corner at y equals one.

6
00:00:19,692 --> 00:00:24,554
From there, plane B reaches the front edge at x equals one, and the quarter mark on

7
00:00:24,554 --> 00:00:29,309
the back edge, which is three quarters back along y: minus three quarters.

8
00:00:29,928 --> 00:00:34,692
Reciprocals: one, minus four thirds, and one over infinity, which is zero.

9
00:00:35,312 --> 00:00:38,201
Multiply by three: three, minus four, zero.

10
00:00:38,821 --> 00:00:41,189
So plane B is three, bar four, zero.

11
00:00:42,789 --> 00:00:45,420
The answer is B: three, bar four, zero.

12
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:49,439
Never write infinity inside Miller indices.

13
00:00:49,439 --> 00:00:53,342
A plane parallel to an axis gets a zero for that axis.

14
00:00:53,342 --> 00:00:56,861
And keep the minus sign after moving the origin.
